<title>USA: IPO FILING -- General Housing Inc.</title>
<headline>IPO FILING -- General Housing Inc.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Company Name		 General Housing Inc</p>
<p>Stock symbol			GENH.O</p>
<p>Estimated price range	   $12-$14/shr</p>
<p>Total shares to be offered    2.0 million</p>
<p>Shrs offered by company	 2.0 million</p>
<p>Shrs outstanding after ipo    5,769,231</p>
<p>Lead Underwriter    Rauscher Pierce Refsnes Inc</p>
<p>Underwriters over-allotment  300,000 shrs</p>
<p>Business: The Waycross, Georgia company produces manufactures homes in the southeast, with an emphasis on value-pricing and enchanged customer service.</p>
<p>Use of Proceeds: redeem all of the shares of the company's reedemable preferred stock, and to reduce indebtedness incurred in the connection with acquisition. The company is the successor to General Manufactured Housing Inc which commenced operations in 1987.</p>
<p>Financial Data in 000s year ended Dec 31:</p>
<p>				  1995		 1994</p>
<p>   - Revenue		 $90,673	    $67,418</p>
<p>   - Net Income	     $4,784	     $2,106</p>
